<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/15th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fall of Granada</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1492">1492</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada-war">Granada War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/granada">Granada</a> was the surrender of the Nasrid kingdom of Granada, the last Muslim state in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iberia">Iberia</a>, to Ferdinand and Isabella in 1492. It completed the Christian reconquest of the peninsula, the final chapter in a process that had accelerated with the collapse of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad Caliphate</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fall-of-granada.jpg" alt="Fall of Granada" width="320" height="205" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Francisco Pradilla y Ortiz · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:La_Rendici%C3%B3n_de_Granada_-_Pradilla.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
